## 2. Vessel Performance Analysis

### 2.1 Fleet Overview

The GML fleet consists of 25 vessels, categorized into three main types: container ships, bulk carriers, and roll-on/roll-off (RoRo) vessels. The following table summarizes the fleet details:

| Vessel Name          | Vessel Type      | Capacity (TEU) | Year Built | Current Location     |
|----------------------|------------------|----------------|------------|-----------------------|
| GML Titan            | Container Ship    | 10,000         | 2018       | Port of Los Angeles    |
| GML Horizon          | Bulk Carrier      | 90,000 MT      | 2016       | Port of Rotterdam      |
| GML Voyager          | RoRo Vessel       | 5,000          | 2020       | Port of Singapore      |
| GML Endeavor         | Container Ship    | 12,000         | 2019       | Port of Hong Kong      |
| GML Discovery        | Bulk Carrier      | 80,000 MT      | 2015       | Port of Shanghai       |

### 2.2 Performance Metrics

For Q3 2023, we recorded the following key performance indicators (KPIs):

| KPI                   | Q2 2023   | Q3 2023   | Change (%) |
|-----------------------|-----------|-----------|------------|
| Average Speed (knots) | 18.5      | 19.0      | +2.7       |
| On-Time Arrival Rate   | 85%       | 90%       | +5.9       |
| Fuel Efficiency (g/TEU)| 150       | 145       | -3.3       |
| Container Turnaround Time (hrs) | 48      | 45       | -6.3       |

### 2.3 Analysis

The increase in on-time arrival rates is attributed to enhanced routing strategies implemented through our partnership with the **Maritime Routing System (MRS)**, which utilizes real-time data to optimize vessel paths. Fuel efficiency improvements are a result of the implementation of eco-friendly technologies on newer vessels such as the GML Endeavor and GML Voyager.

